Package: zenith
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Zenith OS <zenith@localhost>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mohitjoer/Zenith-OS
@RELATIONS@
Description: Zenith OS desktop
 The Zenith session for Ubuntu: a Hyprland configuration, the Quickshell shell
 that draws the bar, dock, launcher, settings and every other window, the
 daemons it talks to, and the control tool that reads machine hardware out of
 sysfs, resolves which hardware profile claims the machine and manages the
 overlay that makes an update safe: a user's override wins at its mirrored path
 and no update can clobber it.
 .
 Quickshell itself is not an archive package. Zenith builds it, and this
 package expects /usr/bin/quickshell to be there.
 .
 This package is configuration data, scripts and binaries. It installs no
 kernel, no bootloader and no driver, it does not touch the login manager, and
 it writes outside /usr/share/zenith/ and /etc/zenith/ only to the fixed places
 listed in docs/architecture.md: the session and portal registrations, the user
 units, the GSettings schemas, the desktop entries and the programs in /usr/bin.
